#: ../../../developer/system/architecture.rst:3
#: 18e99b9be31e4d38801d72c091c50a50
msgid "Architecture"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/architecture.rst:6
#: 4e8bea80d3f54a6a8b38318047df2d31
msgid ""
"Qubes implements a security-by-compartmentalization approach. To do this, "
"Qubes utilizes virtualization technology in order to isolate various "
"programs from each other and even to sandbox many system-level components, "
"such as networking and storage subsystems, so that the compromise of any of "
"these programs or components does not affect the integrity of the rest of "
"the system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/architecture.rst:8
#: 7af8f634d3bb4ae19ece4f7fb30cd79c
msgid "|qubes-schema-v2.png|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/architecture.rst:70
#: 4dd4bd73885c4fc3a703c76566002153
msgid "qubes-schema-v2.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/architecture.rst:10
#: dcada8c372544c6b90226276034669ab
msgid ""
"Qubes lets the user define many secure compartments known as :term:`qubes "
"<qube>`, which are implemented as lightweight :term:`virtual machines (VMs)  "
"<vm>`. For example, the user can have “personal,” “work,” “shopping,” "
"“bank,” and “random” app qubes and can use the applications within those "
"qubes just as if they were executing on the local machine. At the same time, "
"however, these applications are well isolated from each other. Qubes also "
"supports secure copy-and-paste and file sharing between qubes, of course."
msgstr ""

